    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "The rise of digital news consumption has led to a blurring of the lines between what is news and what lies outside it. In this project, I examine existing definitions of news and propose a procedure for identifying a news organization via a mixed-methods case study of the grants committed by the Bill and Melinda Gates Foundation during the COVID-19 pandemic. The procedure is based on the definition of journalism developed by Shapiro (2014). The coding scheme also identifies three subcategories of news organizations: journalistic organizations, non-promotional news republishers, and promotional news organizations.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Kramer, F. (2024). Distinguishing News, Journalism, and Promotional Content in the Digital Age. Version 1. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at https://purl.stanford.edu/qz606sx7251/version/1. https://doi.org/10.25740/qz606sx7251.",
